# Photographs, in development.
#
# Pointed at the deployed Worker rather than a local one: `npm run dev` should
# show the real pictures, because an app full of empty grey frames is unusable
# to develop against. Set VITE_MEDIA_URL=http://localhost:8787 to work against
# the local bucket instead, once images have been put in it.
#
# ── VITE_CONTENT_URL is deliberately absent here, and dev.mjs sets it ───────
#
# It used to be absent full stop, so `npm run dev` read its catalogue from the
# bundled copy and never called the API at all. The reasoning was sound at the
# time: local work should be done against the repo's catalogue and not be
# confused by whatever the Board changed in production this morning.
#
# `npm run dev` now sets it to the local Worker, because the thing being worked
# on is the admin dashboard and whether an edit reaches the app — which cannot
# be seen at all if the app never asks. Note what that costs, since it is no
# longer hypothetical: since the move to Neon there is only ONE database, so
# the rows you see in development are the live ones, and an edit made while
# poking about is an edit the Board will see.
#
# To get the old behaviour for an afternoon — bundled catalogue, no API —
# start the two halves separately: `npm run web:dev` and `npm run api:dev`.
VITE_MEDIA_URL=https://kuk-saarthi-api.indiefluence-in-media.workers.dev
